UPDATE companies SET description='Apparel WorX operates from a 11,000-square-foot facility on Main Street in Wagner, South Dakota. The company was founded in 2014 by Rachel Woods, who began with an in-home embroidery business before expanding into a full-service print shop.

The shop provides custom apparel and promotional products through in-house screen printing (up to seven colors), direct-to-garment printing, embroidery, high-definition transfers, and large-format printing for signs, banners, stickers, and wall clings. Two graphic designers handle custom logo design and brand creation, and the facility also sources promotional items such as tumblers, pens, and koozies. The company reports thousands of custom orders completed annually.

Customers include businesses, schools, sports teams, and organizations across South Dakota and the broader United States. Typical orders range from employee uniforms and spirit wear to fundraiser apparel and event promotional products.

Woods states the goal is to deliver top-notch quality and excellent customer service, turning client ideas into tangible branded products. The company emphasizes in-house production, clear communication, and fast turnaround as its core differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Screen printing (up to 7 colors)", "Direct-to-garment printing", "Embroidery", "Custom logo design", "Promotional product sourcing", "Large format printing (signs, banners, stickers, wall clings)", "High-definition transfers"], "industries": ["Businesses", "Schools", "Organizations", "Sports teams", "Events"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Large format printer"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house production", "Expert graphic designers on staff", "Clear communication", "Fast turnaround", "11,000 sq. ft. production facility"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2014 by Rachel Woods -> /about-us", "Located in Wagner, South Dakota -> /", "11,000 sq. ft. production facility -> /", "Services: screen printing (up to 7 colors), direct-to-garment printing, embroidery, high-definition transfers, large-format printing, custom logo design, promotional product sourcing -> /services", "Serves businesses, schools, organizations across South Dakota and entire United States -> /", "In-house production, expert graphic designers, clear communication, fast turnaround, quality guaranteed -> /", "Large format printer for signs and banners -> /services", "Thousands of custom orders completed -> /", "Goal: top-notch quality and excellent customer service, turning ideas into tangible products -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Started in 2014 by Rachel Woods, Apparel WorX has gone from an in-home embroidery business to a full service print shop located in a newly remodeled 11,000 square foot building.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='apparel-worx' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Arcamed is headquartered in Indianapolis, Indiana. The company was founded in 2012 by Greg Maurer and Kevin Etzkorn after they identified that orthopedic original equipment manufacturers (OEMs) were consistently underserved by their supply chain, facing long lead times, poor quality control, and weak customer service. The pair launched Arcamed to address those gaps with a service-first approach.

Arcamed manufactures surgical case and tray systems, precision caddies for implants, and rigid sterilization containers. The company operates a facility governed by 5S and lean manufacturing principles and employs automated optical assembly inspection, coordinate measuring machines (CMM), Micro‑Vu vision systems, and optical comparators to verify parts. While specific facility size and headcount are not disclosed, the operation supports high‑mix, low‑volume production for medical device customers.

The customer base spans enterprise, mid‑market, and startup orthopedic OEMs. Arcamed positions itself as an extension of its partners’ teams, providing design transfer support and custom branding for sterilization containers. Concrete examples include orthopedic OEMs seeking reliable case‑and‑tray solutions and medical device companies requiring precision caddies.

The founders started Arcamed to eliminate the supply‑chain frustrations they observed in the orthopedic market. The company says its differentiators are concierge‑level service, industry‑lead times, and a relational partnership model rather than transactional selling. It emphasizes that advanced technology and operational expertise work together to deliver world‑class quality and on‑time delivery.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','FDA Registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Surgical case and tray system manufacturing", "Caddy manufacturing", "Rigid sterilization container manufacturing", "Automated optical assembly inspection", "Coordinate measuring (CMM)", "Vision inspection (Micro-Vu)", "Optical comparator inspection", "Lean manufacturing (5S)", "Design transfer support", "Custom branding for sterilization containers"], "industries": ["Orthopedic OEMs", "Medical device OEMs", "Surgical instrument manufacturers"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Automated Optical Assembly Inspection System", "Coordinate Measuring Machine (CMM)", "Vision System (Micro-Vu)", "Optical Comparator"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Concierge-level customer service", "Industry-leading lead times", "99.1% on-time delivery rate", "Relational partnership model", "Integration of advanced inspection technology with lean manufacturing"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Indianapolis, Indiana -> db", "Founded 2012 by Greg Maurer and Kevin Etzkorn -> /about", "Manufactures surgical case & tray systems, caddies, rigid sterilization containers -> /", "ISO 13485:2016 certified and FDA registered -> /, /quality", "Quality equipment: Automated Optical Assembly Inspection System, CMM, Micro-Vu vision system, Optical Comparator -> /quality", "Lean manufacturing and 5S principles -> /", "Serves enterprise, mid-market, and startup orthopedic OEMs -> /about", "Concierge service, industry-leading lead times, on-time delivery (99.1% OTD) -> /about, /", "Relational partnership model -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Your Elite Provider of Surgical Case & Tray Systems", "founded_year": "2012", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='arcamed' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Arch Plastics Packaging, based in Chattanooga, Tennessee, has operated since 1951.

The company manufactures plastic containers primarily for the pharmaceutical and personal care sectors. Its production processes include injection blow molding (IBM) and extrusion blow molding (EBM) for high-density polyethylene (HDPE) bottles, alongside custom molding and custom packaging design. Operations adhere to current Good Manufacturing Practices (cGMP) and a Total Quality Management system, with compliance to 21 CFR 210 and 21 CFR 211. FIFO inventory control and a certificate of compliance accompany each shipment.

Arch Plastics serves the pharmaceutical and personal care industries, supplying containers that meet stringent regulatory requirements. Customers include brands seeking custom packaging solutions that differentiate their products on shelf.

The company states its mission is to produce high-quality pharmaceutical-grade containers while minimizing environmental impact and promoting social governance. It emphasizes versatility, creative quick response, and customer satisfaction as drivers of its growth.', certifications=ARRAY['FDA APPROVED','ANSI','MIL STD','CGMP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection Blow Molding (IBM)", "Extrusion Blow Molding (EBM)", "Custom Molding", "Custom Packaging Design", "cGMP Manufacturing", "Quality Assurance (FIFO, Certificate of Compliance)", "Regulatory Compliance (21 CFR 210/211)"], "industries": ["Pharmaceutical", "Personal Care"], "materials": ["HDPE"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Strict compliance with 21 CFR 210/211 for pharmaceutical manufacturing", "FIFO inventory control for raw materials and finished goods", "Certificate of Compliance and raw material COC documentation with every shipment", "Custom package design and color options for brand differentiation", "Injection blow molding (IBM) and extrusion blow molding (EBM) capabilities for HDPE"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1951 -> db", "Headquartered in Chattanooga, Tennessee -> db, /", "Produces plastic containers for Pharmaceutical and Personal Care Industries -> /", "Follows cGMP and Total Quality Management System -> /", "Certifications: FDA APPROVED, ANSI, MIL STD, CGMP -> db", "Uses Injection Blow Molding (IBM) and Extrusion Blow Molding (EBM) for HDPE products -> /", "Offers custom molded products and custom packaging design -> /", "Complies with 21 CFR 210 and 21 CFR 211 -> /", "Employs FIFO procedures and provides Certificate of Compliance with each shipment -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Arch Plastics Packaging (ARCH) is a reliable producer and supplier of quality plastic containers for the Pharmaceutical and Personal Care Industries.", "founded_year": "1951", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": 