UPDATE companies SET description='Assembled Products, Inc. is based in Rogersville, Alabama, in the Elgin community north of the city. The company was founded in January 1986 by Michael Stevens, who left a larger manufacturer that declined small jobs. Stevens started the business in a former cabinet shop in Collierville, Tennessee, before moving to Piperton, Tennessee in 1990 and later to a 33,000‑square‑foot facility in Elgin, Alabama. The firm is woman‑owned and operates as a small business.

The company provides printed circuit board assembly (PCBA) and electromechanical assembly services, including surface‑mount, through‑hole, and mixed‑technology soldering (both leaded and RoHS‑compliant lead‑free). It handles box‑build and complete system integration, wire‑harness assembly, conformal coating, functional testing, and repair/rework. Additional capabilities encompass design‑for‑manufacturability review, 3D printing, CAD documentation, patent research, and new‑product consulting. The 33,000‑square‑foot Alabama facility supports prototype through medium‑volume runs with a staff of approximately 10.

Named clients have included Federal Express, the University of Memphis, AutoZone, Hypertech, and IBS, alongside individual inventors and hobbyists. The company also serves military electronics upgrade programs and custom electronics projects for clients across Tennessee, Mississippi, Georgia, Florida, and nationally.

