UPDATE companies SET description='AutohausAZ traces its roots to 1979, when it opened as Autohaus Phoenix in Phoenix, Arizona. The business began by supplying European auto parts to local repair shops in the Phoenix valley, initially specializing in Volvo replacement parts and distributing Bosch components.

Today the company operates as a large-scale online distributor of OEM and OE-quality replacement parts for European vehicles, including BMW, Mercedes-Benz, Porsche, Audi, Volkswagen, Volvo, Saab, Land Rover, and Mercedes Sprinter models.

The customer base spans individual do-it-yourselfers and professional repair shops worldwide, with the company serving hundreds of thousands of accounts. Its focus remains on the European automotive aftermarket, providing parts ranging from filters and brake components to engine and transmission components.

AutohausAZ emphasizes direct purchasing to keep prices 20 to 90 percent below retail, backs every part with a three-year/36-month warranty, and offers flexible financing for larger repairs. The combination of a fitment-verified catalog, same-day fulfillment, and a no-hassle return policy is presented as the core differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["OEM and OE-quality parts distribution", "Same-day order fulfillment", "Fitment verification and catalog management", "Customer technical support", "Flexible financing options"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "European vehicle parts distribution", "Automotive repair shops", "DIY automotive"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping for orders placed before 1 PM MST", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1979 as Autohaus Phoenix in Phoenix, Arizona -> /about-us", "Operates nationwide warehouse network with same-day shipping before 1 PM MST -> /about-us", "Distributes OEM/OE-quality parts for BMW, Mercedes, Porsche, Audi, VW, Volvo, Saab, Land Rover, Sprinter -> /", "Offers 3-year/36-month warranty on all parts -> /", "Serves DIYers and professional repair shops worldwide -> /about-us", "Headquarters Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "Direct purchasing to offer 20-90% off retail -> /about-us", "Fitment-verified catalog maintained by specialists -> /", "Flexible financing available -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "AutohausAZ began in 1979 as Autohaus Phoenix, providing European auto parts to local repair shops in the Phoenix, Arizona area.", "founded_year": "1979", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='autohausaz' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Autokiniton’s Greenville operation is part of a global automotive supplier formed in May 2018 when KPS Capital Partners and George Thanopoulos created Autokiniton Global Group (AGG) to acquire L&W Group, a Tier 1 specialist in metal stampings, welded assemblies, and tubular products. The combined entity, headquartered in Fountain Inn, South Carolina, grew through the September 2019 acquisition of Tower International, creating the second-largest body-in-white and vehicle-frame supplier in North America with $2.3 billion in annual sales.

The company manufactures high-strength structural components and precision stampings for vehicle bodies and frames. Additional capabilities include tube forming on three mills, roll forming on two mills, laser cutting with 40 lasers, and custom tool and die development.

Autokiniton serves the automotive industry as a Tier 1 supplier to the world’s automakers, including Ford (which awarded it a World Excellence Award in 2021). Its propulsion-agnostic components go into electric vehicles, internal-combustion cars, minivans, and pickup trucks. The company also supplies tubing for the trailer and recreational-vehicle markets.

The firm emphasizes streamlined, bureaucracy-free problem solving and strategic plant placement near customer assembly sites to reduce logistics costs. Its differentiation rests on joining dissimilar metals (aluminum, hot-formed and ultra-high-strength steels) at scale, backed by a quality lab performing crush, tensile, and metallurgical testing.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Gas metal arc welding (MIG)", "Resistance spot welding", "Capacitive discharge welding", "Drawn arc welding", "Laser welding", "Friction stir welding", "Complex assembly and body-in-white assembly", "Tube forming (induction resistance welded)", "Roll forming", "Cold stamping (single-stage, progressive, tandem, transfer)", "Hot stamping", "Laser cutting", "Tool and die development", "Servo press forming", "Roller hemming"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Trailer", "Recreational vehicle"], "materials": ["Steel", "Aluminum", "Hot-formed steel", "High-strength steel", "Ultra-high-strength steel (UHSS)", "Boron coated steel"], "equipment": ["1,200+ MIG welding robots", "3,000+ spot welding/material handling robots", "3 tube mills", "2 roll form mills", "214 tandem presses (up to 3,000 tons)", "40 transfer presses (up to 3,000 tons)", "105 progressive presses (up to 1,600 tons)", "8 hot stamp lines with 23 laser units", "40 hot stamp presses (1,000\u20133,000 tons, 108\"\u2013288\" beds)", "40 laser cutting machines (1,000 lb capacity)", "Servo presses for aluminum and steel"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Strategic plant placement near customer assembly plants to expedite logistics and reduce costs", "Streamlined processes that reduce operating costs and increase agility", "Large-scale joining of dissimilar metals including aluminum, hot-formed and ultra-high-strength steels", "Ford World Excellence Award recipient (2021)"], "facts_used": ["Founded May 2018 by KPS Capital Partners and George Thanopoulos -> /services", "Acquisition of L&W Group May 2018 -> /services", "Acquisition of Tower International completed September 2019 -> /services, /", "Headquarters Fountain Inn, SC -> db", "8.3 million sq ft manufacturing space -> /about, /services", "36 U.S. manufacturing & design facilities, 4 in Mexico, 1 in Brazil, 1 tech facility in India -> /services", "Cold stamping: 214 tandem presses, 40 transfer presses, 105 progressive presses -> /about", "Hot stamping: 8 lines, 23 laser units, 40 presses 1,000-3,000 tons -> /about", "Welding: 1,200+ MIG robots, 3,000+ spot welding robots -> /about", "Tube forming: 3 tube mills, 2 roll form mills -> /about", "Laser cutting: 40 lasers, 1,000 lb capacity -> /about", "Industries: automotive, trailer, recreational vehicle -> /about", "Ford World Excellence Award December 2021 -> /", "Propulsion-agnostic components for EVs, ICE, minivans, pickups -> /", "Strategic plant placement near customers -> /services", "Streamlined solutions philosophy -> /services", "Joining dissimilar metals (aluminum, hot-formed, high-strength steel) -> /about", "Quality lab: crush & cone tests, metallurgical etching, tensile testing, hardness testing -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We manufacture full body-frame structural assemblies that provide state-of-the-art lightweighting and structural benefits.", "founded_year": "2018", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='autokiniton-greenville' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Autoliv North America Inc is headquartered in Ogden, Utah. The company operates as the North American arm of Autoliv, a global automotive safety supplier with operations in 25 countries and 13 technical centers worldwide. No founding year or founder names are provided in the public materials.

Autoliv develops, manufactures, and markets passive safety systems including airbags, seatbelts, and steering wheels for virtually all major automotive manufacturers. The company also produces mobility safety solutions such as a wearable airbag vest for motorcycle riders, developed in collaboration with gear maker RS Taichi. Its product portfolio includes pyrotechnical safety switches for short-circuit prevention, the HBM Safety Suite, and components critical to airbag ignition and deployment. Autoliv operates 13 technical centers with 20 test tracks and offers specialized test services tailored to industry needs. The global workforce numbers approximately 64,000 employees, and the company reported $10.8 billion in net sales for 2025 with a 44 percent market share.

The primary customers are automotive OEMs across passenger and commercial vehicle segments. Autoliv also serves the motorcycle safety market through partnerships with riding-gear manufacturers like RS Taichi. Recent collaborations include agreements with XPENG and Great Wall Motor to advance safer mobility worldwide. The company’s safety solutions address the entire mobility chain, from traditional vehicles to emerging multi-modal transport.

Autoliv states its vision as "Saving More Lives," with a long-standing ambition for its products to save 100,000 lives per year and to achieve carbon-neutral operations by 2030. The company emphasizes digitalization and automation as cornerstones of operational excellence, and highlights its history of delivering virtually all major technological breakthroughs in automotive safety.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Airbag manufacturing", "Seatbelt manufacturing", "Steering wheel manufacturing", "Mobility safety solutions development", "Test services", "Pyrotechnical safety switch production", "HBM Safety Suite deployment", "Wearable airbag vest development", "Airbag ignition and deployment component manufacturing", "Virtual testing", "Digitalization and automation integration"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Motorcycle", "Commercial Vehicle", "Mobility Safety"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["World''s largest automotive safety supplier with operations in 25 countries", "13 technical centers and 20 test tracks worldwide", "Products saved an estimated 40,000 lives in 2025", "44% global market share in automotive safety systems", "Wearable airbag vest for motorcycle riders developed with RS Taichi"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Ogden, Utah -> db", "World''s largest automotive safety supplier with operations in 25 countries and 13 Tech Centers -> /", "Develop, manufacture, market protective systems: airbags, seatbelts, steering wheels -> /about-us", "Mobility safety solutions including wearable airbag vest for motorcycle riders -> /about-us, db", "Collaboration with RS Taichi for motorcycle airbag vest -> db", "Pyrotechnical safety switches for short-circuit prevention -> /", "HBM Safety Suite -> /", "Components for airbag ignition and deployment -> /about-us", "13 technical centers with 20 test tracks -> /about-us", "Test services tailored for industry needs -> db", "~64,0